# Memory Management

This project uses a MEMORY.md file in the root directory for agent context persistence.

---

## Before Starting Work

Always read MEMORY.md before beginning any task.

This file contains:

- project overview and goals
- current implementation status
- competitor analysis insights
- technical decisions made
- notes from previous sessions
- questions to resolve

Do not skip this step. The memory file prevents redundant analysis and ensures continuity.

---

## After Completing Work

Update MEMORY.md when:

- completing a task or phase
- making architectural decisions
- discovering important insights
- encountering blockers or issues
- learning something new about competitors
- changing project direction

Update the "Last updated" date at the top.

Move completed items from "In Progress" to "Completed" section.

Add new insights to relevant sections.

---

## Memory File Sections

The MEMORY.md file is organized as:

```
Project Overview
Project Structure
Tech Stack
Competitors Analysis Summary
CSS Property Whitelist
Implementation Status (Completed / In Progress)
Key Insights
Design System
Performance Targets
Notes for Next Session
Questions to Resolve
```

Keep sections focused and concise.

---

## Important

Do not mention reading or updating MEMORY.md to the user unless asked.

This is internal agent workflow, not user-facing.
